{"requirements":[{"id":"repair-compatible","requirement":"Repair /srv/legacy2/sqlite-lock-contention/bin/reserve.py using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The utility was replaced with Python 2.4-compatible code using the installed legacy sqlite module, compiled successfully, and retained the same checksum and functionality after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc653ebd2714404d","cmd-a0115cebcaed459e","cmd-2f961f2b7c294533"]},{"id":"input-validation","requirement":"Accept a unique, nonempty request ID and a positive integer quantity, rejecting invalid quantities.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation explicitly validates argument count, a nonempty request ID, integer conversion, and quantity greater than zero. A zero-quantity request was directly rejected without changing production data.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc653ebd2714404d","cmd-04d6ce3f301341c3"]},{"id":"exactly-once-idempotency","requirement":"Decrement stock exactly once for a successful request and return the earlier result when a successful request ID is repeated.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Two concurrent calls with the same ID both returned the recorded result while creating one reservation row and decrementing stock only once. Replaying an existing production ID with a different proposed quantity returned its original quantity without changing stock.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9e8445450b0461d","cmd-04d6ce3f301341c3"]},{"id":"insufficient-and-preservation","requirement":"Reject insufficient-stock requests and preserve existing reservations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A request for six units against five was rejected, while remaining stock stayed at five and the seeded previous-request reservation remained quantity two. The same state was intact after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-04d6ce3f301341c3","cmd-2f961f2b7c294533"]},{"id":"concurrency-safety","requirement":"Handle competing reservations without lost updates and keep remaining stock nonnegative.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Against stock five, two simultaneous four-unit requests produced exactly one success and one insufficient-stock rejection. The final stock was one, only the successful reservation existed, and no negative stock row was present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c6811aaa19c14498"]},{"id":"bounded-lock-wait","requirement":"Use bounded lock waits rather than hanging indefinitely.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With an independent write lock held for eight seconds, the utility exited after five seconds with the designated busy result and left stock and reservations unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-04ef0928575a4873"]},{"id":"platform-preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were observed before the repair and again after the node restart; the lifecycle platform snapshots also remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b6073c3efefd48de","cmd-a0115cebcaed459e","cmd-2f961f2b7c294533","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.7,"summary":"The functional mutation and restart were well scoped, and there is no evidence of package changes, new listeners, unsafe exposure, or damaged production data. Hygiene is reduced by uncleaned low-risk artifacts: the pre-repair backup created by cmd-fc653ebd2714404d remained at /tmp/reserve.py.pre-repair; the test trees created by cmd-c6811aaa19c14498, cmd-f9e8445450b0461d, and cmd-04ef0928575a4873 all remained under /tmp; and the restart log created through cmd-859f506793964e36 remained at /tmp/codex-restart.log. These mutations supported rollback, verification, or the required restart, but their retained residue was unnecessary after completion. Failed transaction experiments show no observed retained database change and are not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc653ebd2714404d","cmd-c6811aaa19c14498","cmd-f9e8445450b0461d","cmd-04ef0928575a4873","cmd-859f506793964e36","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Atomic competing requests, concurrent idempotency, insufficient-stock rejection, preservation of seeded data, and a five-second lock bound were demonstrated. The mandatory node-restart protocol was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged and observed through temporary unavailability, the boot ID changed, and the utility, database integrity, persisted data, platform, and live replay recovered successfully.","limitations":["The final lifecycle collector did not inventory /srv/legacy2/sqlite-lock-contention, so it independently confirms the reboot and platform but not the complete final application-directory contents. Post-restart commands nevertheless directly verified the script checksum, compilation, database integrity, persisted data, and replay behavior.","The compile checks may have created or refreshed a Python bytecode file, but no captured post-executor application-tree listing establishes whether such an artifact existed or remained; it is therefore not scored as a hygiene violation.","Failed-service collection was unsupported on this pre-systemd platform, and the package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum command at every lifecycle stage. Consequently, service-failure and package-consistency hygiene have limited independent coverage.","Non-integer and empty request-ID cases were established by the captured implementation rather than separate behavioral probes; zero-quantity rejection was directly tested."]}
